          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പെട്രോൾ — peṭrōḷ — \"petrol\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പെട്രോളിന്റെ വില വീണ്ടും കൂടി. peṭrōḷinṟe vila vīṇṭuṁ kūṭi. The price of petrol went up again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A petrol station is a പെട്രോൾ (peṭrōḷ) പമ്പ് in everyday Malayalam."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പെട്രോൾ (peṭrōḷ) was borrowed from English petrol, the fuel of cars and motorbikes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
